From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Let the rate control spend where the picture needs it

A cast holding a constant rate on a link with little room was found to drop
nothing at all and still look wrong: the picture swung between sharp and soft
as what was on screen moved, worst wherever a window scrolled. No frame was
late, none was lost, and every one of them was the size it was asked to be.

Within a frame, the whole picture is held to one quantiser, so a cost
concentrated in one corner is paid by coarsening all of it. Macroblock level
rate control lets the bits go where the picture needs them, and this encoder
has it in every mode but the one this is not.

The buffer the rate control may borrow across was widened here too, from two
frames to four, and taken out again: it is latency on a link that has little
to spare, and it was never judged on its own because it arrived in the same
patch as this and on an evening when nothing looked good anyway. Two frames
is what the encoder keeps.

Periodic intra refresh, which spreads the cost of recovery rather than
spending it on one frame, is the third thing and does not exist here. The VA
low power entrypoint does not offer it, and a shorter distance between
keyframes is no substitute: it makes that spike arrive more often rather than
smaller. Where it matters more than hardware encoding does, the encoder that
has it is the software one.

diff -ruN a/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c b/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
--- a/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
+++ b/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
@@ -1135,6 +1135,15 @@
       if (vbv_kbit > 0)
         g_object_set (encoder, "cpb-size", vbv_kbit, NULL);
 
+      /* Let the rate control move bits about inside a frame rather than
+       * holding the whole of it to one quantiser. A frame whose cost is all
+       * in one corner otherwise has the entire picture coarsened to pay for
+       * it, which is seen as the whole screen going soft when one window
+       * scrolls. Not available in constant quantiser mode, which this is
+       * not. */
+      if (g_object_class_find_property (G_OBJECT_GET_CLASS (encoder), "mbbrc"))
+        g_object_set (encoder, "mbbrc", 1, NULL);
+
       g_message ("WfdMediaFactory: Encoding on the processor's own graphics.");
       break;
 
